    "FUNC.PERMUTATIONA"
  ],
  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "PERMUTATIONA checks number < 0 before truncation (-1 < number_chosen < 0 becomes 0) and uses decimal 10^k at base 10",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, PERMUTATIONA(number, number_chosen) rejects raw number < 0 before truncation (so PERMUTATIONA(-0.9999999999999987, 1) is #NUM!), whereas number_chosen in (-1, 0] truncates to 0 and returns 1. Both arguments are bounded below 2,147,483,647. When truncated number == 10, Excel takes decimal power conversion ten_to(k) (#NUM! for k > 308); otherwise it runs x87-stored repeated squaring. Under compat-1, @PERMUTATIONA returns #NAME?.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0 build 20430 (71,915/71,915 full-bank and 120/120 pinned PERMUTATIONA rows) and 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (row 180).",
